\ cm/rt-cm.4 - the command model's runtime, step 1 of its prototype (855): local slots the
\ collector sees, upvalues, blocks. docs/COMMAND-MODEL.md, "The runtime plan" - a draft's
\ prototype. Loaded on rill2's image (rt.4's arena and collector, rill2's D- words);
\ tests/cm/ drives it. A front end comes later; this is what it will compile to.

7 CONSTANT K-BLOCK   8 CONSTANT K-UPV

\ ---- local slots: a def's frame, where the collector can see it ----
\ Each FRAME saves the frame below as a tagged number - odd, which the collector passes by - and
\ adds n slots, none set. A safe point inside a def is safe when its values are here, not on a
\ Forth stack.
4096 CONSTANT LS-MAX
LS-MAX CELLS BUFFER: LS   VARIABLE LS#   VARIABLE FP
: FRAME ( n --- )
  LS# @ OVER + 1+ LS-MAX > IF S" cm: frames too deep" R-FAIL THEN
  FP @ 2* 1+  LS LS# @ CELLS + !  1 LS# +!  LS# @ FP !
  LS LS# @ CELLS + OVER CELLS ERASE  LS# +! ;               \ the n slots cleared at once (867)
: UNFRAME ( --- )   FP @ 1- DUP LS# !  CELLS LS + @ 2/ FP ! ;
: LS@ ( i --- item )   FP @ + CELLS LS + @ ;
: LS! ( item i --- )   FP @ + CELLS LS + ! ;
VARIABLE MFP                                       \ the main frame's, a script's or the prompt's (884): a def
: MLS@ ( i --- item )   MFP @ + CELLS LS + @ ;    \ reads and sets the script's variables in it
: MLS! ( item i --- )   MFP @ + CELLS LS + ! ;

\ ---- upvalues: a captured variable's cell, shared by its frame and the blocks that captured it ----
: UPV-NEW ( item --- upv )   1 CELLS R-ALLOT  TUCK !  K-UPV R-BOX ;
: UPV@ ( upv --- item )   CELL+ @ @ ;
: UPV! ( item upv --- )   CELL+ @ ! ;

\ ---- blocks: code and what it captured; run with its captures at hand ----
\ A block: [xt][n][capture 0]..[capture n-1], each capture an item - an upvalue for a variable
\ captured by reference. ENVS holds the blocks running, innermost last; the collector sees them.
: BLK-NEW ( c0 .. cn-1 n xt --- block )
  OVER 2 + CELLS R-ALLOT >R  R@ !  DUP R@ CELL+ !
  BEGIN DUP WHILE 1-  TUCK  R@ 2 CELLS + SWAP CELLS + !  REPEAT DROP
  R> K-BLOCK R-BOX ;
256 CONSTANT ENV-MAX
ENV-MAX CELLS BUFFER: ENVS   VARIABLE ENV#
: E@ ( i --- item )   ENVS ENV# @ 1- CELLS + @  2 CELLS +  SWAP CELLS + @ ;
: BLK-CALL ( i*x block --- j*x )   \ rule 11's block: run it
  DUP D-KIND K-BLOCK <> IF S" cm: not a block" R-FAIL THEN
  CELL+ @  ENV# @ ENV-MAX < 0= IF S" cm: blocks too deep" R-FAIL THEN
  DUP ENVS ENV# @ CELLS + !  1 ENV# +!
  LS# @ >R  FP @ >R  @ CATCH  R> R> ROT                    \ a block with a frame of its own (858):
  ?DUP IF  >R  LS# !  FP !  -1 ENV# +!  R> THROW  THEN      \ a throw through it puts the frames back
  2DROP  -1 ENV# +! ;

\ ---- the collector: the two new kinds, and the new roots ----
: G-UPV ( u --- u' )   DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN
  1 CELLS G-MOVE  DUP @ G-BOX OVER ! ;
: G-BLOCK ( b --- b' )   DUP G-IN? 0= IF EXIT THEN  DUP G-FWD? IF @ EXIT THEN
  DUP CELL+ @ 2 + CELLS G-MOVE
  DUP CELL+ @ 0 ?DO  DUP 2 CELLS + I CELLS +  DUP @ G-BOX SWAP !  LOOP ;
: G-COPY-CM ( a kind --- a' )
  DUP K-BLOCK = IF DROP G-BLOCK EXIT THEN  DUP K-UPV = IF DROP G-UPV EXIT THEN  G-COPY-IMPL ;
' G-COPY-CM IS G-COPY
: G-PTR-CM ( kind --- f )   DUP K-BLOCK = OVER K-UPV = OR IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  G-PTR-KIND-IMPL ;
' G-PTR-CM IS G-PTR-KIND?
: G-MORE-CM ( --- )   \ the frames' slots, and the blocks running
  LS# @ 0 ?DO  LS I CELLS + DUP @ G-BOX SWAP !  LOOP
  ENV# @ 0 ?DO  ENVS I CELLS + DUP @ G-BLOCK SWAP !  LOOP ;
' G-MORE-CM IS G-MORE
